# ===========================================================================
# CityParquet monorepo.
#
# Each subtree keeps its own .gitignore for what is local to it (Cargo
# artefacts in lib/*, node_modules in documents/, the database harness's
# data/ and .venv/). What lives here is what spans them — above all the
# benchmark tree, whose code and evidence sit in different directories.
# ===========================================================================

# --- benchmark corpora and derived artefacts -------------------------------
#
# ~24 GB of city models, all fetched from pinned URLs with pinned byte sizes
# by `just fetch-data` / `just fetch-3dbag`. The pins live in
# benchmark/scripts/fetch_benchmark.sh and benchmark/formats/
# corpus_urls.txt, both committed — the bytes themselves never were.
#
# A trailing "/" pattern only matches an actual directory, never a symlink
# (even one pointing at a directory) — see `git help gitignore`. Benchmark
# runs sometimes point this path at a sibling clone's corpus via a symlink
# (`ln -s .../data benchmark/formats/data`), so a second, slash-less entry
# below the directory rule is required to ignore the symlink itself.
/benchmark/formats/data/
/benchmark/formats/data

# External converters fetched by `just fetch-tools` (citygml-tools). The PINS
# live in benchmark/scripts/fetch_tools.sh, which IS committed; the
# unpacked ~28 MB of JARs is not.
/benchmark/formats/tools/

# benchviz's default output directory when run without `--out`
# (bench_data.json, index.html, figures/): all of it is derived from the
# results CSVs and regenerates in seconds.
/benchmark/summary/

# benchmark/plot's own uv-managed venv + Python bytecode cache — its source
# (pyproject.toml, *.py, uv.lock) IS committed.
/benchmark/plot/.venv/

# --- shared -----------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store

# --- local agent tooling ----------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.codex/
.opencode/
.superpowers/
.claudian/
apm_modules/
ai/skills/

# scripts/catalog2cityparquet's own uv-managed venv — its source
# (pyproject.toml, *.py, uv.lock) IS committed.
/scripts/catalog2cityparquet/.venv/
# benchmark/readbench is its own Cargo workspace.
/benchmark/readbench/target/
.worktrees/

.agents/

# Generated benchmark inputs, raw evidence and rendered summaries. The
# full-profile result directories and the full summary are re-included here so
# that the evidence of a host run shows up in git status and can be committed;
# none is committed until that run.
/benchmark/runs/*
!/benchmark/runs/databases/
/benchmark/runs/databases/*
!/benchmark/runs/databases/results/
!/benchmark/runs/formats/
/benchmark/runs/formats/*
!/benchmark/runs/formats/results/
!/benchmark/runs/formats/bloom_results/
!/benchmark/runs/summary/
/benchmark/runs/summary/*
!/benchmark/runs/summary/full/
